      "prompt": "Write a TypeScript function named `fetchUserProfile` that takes a userId string, calls an external API, and safely handles network timeouts or 500 errors using try/catch. Include explicit type annotations for the return type.\n",
      "rawOutput": "```typescript\n// Define the UserProfile interface\ninterface UserProfile {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n  avatarUrl?: string;\n  createdAt: string;\n}\n\n// Define the API response type\ninterface ApiResponse {\n  success: boolean;\n  data?: UserProfile;\n  error?: string;\n}\n\n/**\n * Fetches a user profile from an external API.\n * @param userId - The unique identifier of the user\n * @returns A Promise that resolves to the user profile or throws an error\n * @throws Error if the request times out, fails with 500 status, or encounters network issues\n */\nexport async function fetchUserProfile(userId: string): Promise<UserProfile> {\n  const controller = new AbortController();\n  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000); // 5 second timeout\n\n  try {\n    const response = await fetch(`https://api.example.com/users/${userId}`, {\n      method: 'GET',\n      headers: {\n        'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n      },\n      signal: controller.signal,\n    });\n\n    clearTimeout(timeoutId);\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n      if (response.status === 500) {\n        throw new Error('Server error: Unable to fetch user profile');\n      }\n      throw new Error(`HTTP error: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}`);\n    }\n\n    const data: ApiResponse = await response.json();\n\n    if (!data.success || !data.data) {\n      throw new Error('Failed to retrieve user profile data');\n    }\n\n    return data.data;\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error instanceof Error) {\n      if (error.name === 'AbortError') {\n        throw new Error('Request timed out');\n      }\n      throw error;\n    }\n    throw new Error('An unexpected error occurred');\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis function:\n\n- Accepts a `userId` string and returns a `Promise<UserProfile>`\n- Uses `AbortController` to enforce a 5-second timeout\n- Handles HTTP 500 errors and other non-success responses explicitly\n- Uses `try/catch` to manage network and parsing errors\n- Includes clear, explicit type annotations for all parameters and return values\n- Throws descriptive errors to aid debugging and error handling in the calling code",
